  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trust Funds Contributions to support the implementation of the zambia social cash transfer programme as a 25% contribution ICF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing technical support in managing the ministry of community development.  The original expected outcome of the programme was a national SCT programme reaching 350,000 households. The SCT programme now has country wide coverage reaching more than 1,100,000 households (69% women and 9% households with people with disabilities), with an average household of five people (LCMS 2016, awaiting new data from LCMS and Census 2022) it is estimated that the programme currently reaches 5.5 million people. b4)	Cooperating partners that recently joined the sector include Ireland (in 2020), Switzerland (2022) and Germany, through KFW (2020 for Covid ECTs, then 2022 for wider social protection support), supporting both direct transfers and the technical assistance components of the programme</narrative>
  </description>
